netically normal embryo  if someone has a genetic problem in  their family like a disorder that many  people have had  or if we do genetic blood tests on a  male and a female  or even on a lesbian couple in the  future sperm donor or the opposite for a  gay couple and  a future egg donor if two people who are  going to reproduce with each other  do carry a genetic disorder this is now  not a chromosomal problem but a disorder  like cystic fibrosis sickle cell  disorder we can then do a special test  on their embryo  to make sure that the embryo that's  going to be transferred into the female  no longer has the diseased embryo going  in  and only has a carrier like the parent  or completely healthy without even being  a carrier state embryo  wow so you can get rid of genetic  disorders  some of them anyway basically as long as  they have been  linked to a chromosome we can go ahead  and  find them so sadly like autism has not  been linked  to a chromosome it's something that just  happens diabetes  hypertension has not but certain cancers  like braca one and brachipat ii breast  cancer  cancers have been linked and we are able  to  so if you have braca in your body and  you have a higher  way higher risk of breast cancer ovarian  cancer in the future  and you don't want to pass that on to  your child we are able to check to see  which embryo does not carry the bracha  gene  and then only transfers those back and a  lot of people do that  wow um okay so how do you look at how do  you look for healthy sperm what does  that look like  so when it comes to sperm we look for  sperm that has  um is motile in a moving well we look  for the sperm  counts that are high we also look for  the quality of the sperm which is  called morphology it's the normal forms  of sperm  and we look to see that the sperm has a  normal head  a normal neck and a normal tail that's  pretty much as much as we can do right  now we also have a technology in our  office called zymot zymot  the zymot 